  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_silent",
      "name": {
        "en": "Silence's Badge",
        "zh": "赫默证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_silent",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Silence has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for healing teammates in the field.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Medic Operator during field operations to exercise Medic responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员赫默擅长在战场上为干员提供治疗\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为医疗干员，行使医师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_silent",
      "name": {
        "en": "Emergency Self-Defense Procedures",
        "zh": "紧急防卫程序",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_silent",
      "description": {
        "en": "'You want me to add a self-defense module to your medical drones?'\nOutside the Lutra Workshop, Magallan stares wide-eyed at Silence, as if she's looking at a Seaborn flopping about in the middle of the great tundra.\n'Um... would it be strange?'\n'Not really, if you think about it—I just never imagined it, that's all. I figured you'd rather improve its healing efficacy, or maybe durability.'\n'I probably would have thought along those lines in the past, yes.'\nMagallan doesn't say anything. She may spend her days in the tundra year in and year out, but that doesn't mean she's completely clueless about Rhine Lab's internal affairs.\n'I initially wanted nothing more than to be a researcher. I sought to thoroughly analyze the relationship between Originium and life, and I assumed I'd pry open the boundaries of knowledge with my own two hands.\n'But following a string of incidents, I could no longer ignore this: as long as my research doesn't change course, I will never be able to completely exclude the 'human' perspective.\n'Before I started a new job, I first needed to stand in the shoes of a doctor, from where I could examine my own dreams and ambitions. The most basic respect you can afford someone, as I see it.\n'Those drones, then, are the crystallization of my ideology.'\nThe two inadvertently share a glance towards the workshop. Mayer is inside racking her brains; entering hastily was very liable to get you bitten.\n'Speaking as a layman in medicine, I think these drones are already perfect as an extension of a doctor's hands.'\n'Perhaps, but I've increasingly come to realize that merely serving as a doctor... is still not enough.'\nSilence's expression is complicated. She lightly touches her hair.\n'Humans are far more complex than Originium.\n'We can roughly determine Originium activity from its surface appearance. We can predict the ETA of Catastrophes from natural phenomena. We can avoid infection through highly effective protective measures.\n'But how do we determine a person's interior life from what's visible to us? Do falling figures signify deterioration or improvement? Are people with crossbows ultimately there to defend, or to kill?'\n'Just like a snowfield that seems perfectly quiet,' Magallan murmurs to herself.\n'Yes, just like a snowfield that seems perfectly quiet.\n'Therefore, I need tougher measures, so that when the snowfield finally bares its fangs at me, I can protect the people I should be protecting.'",
        "zh": "“给你的医疗无人机加装防卫模块？”\n鲁特拉工作室门外，麦哲伦瞪大眼睛看着赫默，仿佛在无尽的冰原中央看到一只活蹦乱跳的海嗣。\n“嗯……很奇怪？”\n“仔细想想，倒也没有很奇怪，只是单纯的没想到而已。我以为你更希望增强无人机的治疗效率或者耐用程度。”\n“如果是之前的我，大概也会这么想吧。”\n麦哲伦没有说话。她成年累月地跟冰原打交道，但这并不意味着她对莱茵生命内部发生的事情一无所知。\n“最初，我只想当一个研究者。我要彻底解析源石与生命间的关系，我要用自己的双手开拓知识的边界。\n“在一系列事件之后，我终于无法再忽视这一点：只要我的研究不改变方向，我就永远无法把‘人’从我的理念里排除出去。\n“在开始新的工作之前，我必须首先站在一名医生的立场上审视自己的梦想和野心。在我看来，这是对人最基本的尊重。\n“那些无人机就是我当时想法的结晶。”\n两人不约而同往工作室方向看了一眼。梅尔正在里面绞尽脑汁，贸然进去很可能会被咬。\n“在我这个医疗上的外行看来，作为医生双手的延伸，这些无人机已经很完美了。”\n“也许吧，但我越来越意识到，仅仅成为一个医生……仍然不够。”\n赫默表情复杂，理了理自己的头发。\n“人比源石复杂太多了。\n“我们能从外表大致判断出源石的活性，能从自然现象预测天灾来临的时间，能用行之有效的防护手段让自己免于感染。\n“但我们该如何从一个人可见的部分判断他的内在？下降的指标意味着恶化还是好转，拿着弩的人究竟是护卫还是杀手？”\n“就像表面平静的雪原。”麦哲伦喃喃自语。\n“是啊，就像表面平静的雪原。\n“所以，我需要一些更强硬的手段，让我能在这片雪原对我露出獠牙时保护该保护的人。”",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
